+
+<!-- SECTION:PLAN:BEGIN -->
+1. Confirm the mechanism: Enter schedules the visible send with app.call_later, so Textual's App.on_callback awaits the whole send -- and a slash command's handler (/generate-video: cost confirm, generation, storage choice) -- on the APP pump that reads every key; the Send button awaits the same send on the Console pump (Stop button, Console keys dead). Prove it with mounted tests that fail on origin/dev on a bounded pump-runs poll (driver-style keys, like TASK-33621.28's test), not by inference.
+2. Red tests first (bootstrap_profile): ConsoleHarness /generate-video via Enter and via Send button, paid backend + cost confirm: app pump and Console pump keep running while the confirm is up; Escape cancels with no generation started and the draft kept; F1/Ctrl+Q consumed. Generation in flight (blocked stub at the adapter seam): both pumps run, F1 opens help, Stop reaches the cancel event. Storage choice reached via Enter answers keys. Real TldwCli: Enter-sent /generate-video, Ctrl+Q under the cost confirm reaches the quit flow; Ctrl+Q under the storage choice still asks 'Discard generated video and quit?'.
